WEBVTT

1
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.957
(rattles)

2
00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:46.254
ROSÉ (in English):
<i>How it all started? That's a big question.</i>

3
00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:51.134
<i>I think everybody
has like a different start</i>

4
00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.720
<i>to how they got to this one place</i>

5
00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:57.057
<i>where we all kind of got together
to create BLACKPINK.</i>

6
00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.142
<i>But me, personally,</i>

7
00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.103
<i>I came through just a simple audition</i>

8
00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:05.857
<i>and ended up practicing
at YG Entertainment</i>

9
00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.610
<i>for about four years, I think it was.</i>

10
00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.614
<i>I'm the newest member
out of all four of us.</i>

11
00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:15.909
<i>All I remember is practicing a lot,</i>

12
00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.120
<i>having a very strong drive,</i>

13
00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:21.372
<i>and a big goal ahead of us.</i>

14
00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:25.460
<i>It took a long time, but we made it...</i>
(chuckles)

15
00:01:25.543 --> 00:01:27.670
<i>...and we debuted as BLACKPINK.</i>

16
00:01:30.173 --> 00:01:31.591
(audience cheering)

17
00:01:31.674 --> 00:01:34.552
ANNOUNCER (in Korean): <i>YG's new girl group
BLACKPINK set a new record</i>

18
00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:35.720
<i>by reaching number one</i>

19
00:01:35.804 --> 00:01:38.973
<i>in a network television music program
in just 14 days after their debut.</i>

20
00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:39.933
<i>They have 27 videos,</i>

21
00:01:40.016 --> 00:01:42.268
<i>including the music video
for</i> DDU-DU DDU-DU,

22
00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:43.937
<i>with hundreds of millions of views...</i>

23
00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.396
<i>Setting various records...</i>

24
00:01:46.147 --> 00:01:47.899
<i>Surpassing the global pop stars...</i>

25
00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:50.610
WOMAN: <i>What is in store...</i>

26
00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:53.947
ANNOUNCER: <i>BLACKPINK is finally having
their first concert in Jamsil</i>

27
00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.865
<i>in their second year since their debut...</i>

28
00:01:56.407 --> 00:01:58.618
BLACKPINK (in Korean):
Hello, we are BLACKPINK.

29
00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:02.038
ANNOUNCER: <i>BLACKPINK started off
their world tour with their first concert.</i>

30
00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:05.375
<i>January 31st, 2021, BLACKPINK celebrates
the 5th anniversary of their debut.</i>

31
00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.669
<i>They welcome fans around the world
with online concerts...</i>

32
00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:09.879
ANNOUNCER (in English):
<i>Our next guests are multi-platinum selling</i>

33
00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.507
<i>and chart-topping K-pop girl group
you know.</i>

34
00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.634
MALE ANNOUNCER: <i>Please welcome BLACKPINK!</i>

35
00:02:14.717 --> 00:02:16.928
(audience cheering)

36
00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.724
ANNOUNCER (in Korean):
<i>Fans around the world are looking forward</i>

37
00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:25.019
<i>to seeing BLACKPINK in person
to celebrate their 5th anniversary.</i>

38
00:02:30.775 --> 00:02:33.194
(<i>Ddu-Du Ddu-Du</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

39
00:02:37.532 --> 00:02:40.034
(audience cheering)

40
00:04:32.981 --> 00:04:35.441
(<i>Ddu-Du Ddu-Du</i> continues)

41
00:06:08.576 --> 00:06:11.079
(audience cheer)

42
00:06:14.415 --> 00:06:17.585
(humming)

43
00:06:22.006 --> 00:06:24.634
(audience cheering)

44
00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.846
(explosion)

45
00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:31.099
(<i>Ddu-Du Ddu-Du</i> continues)

46
00:06:38.022 --> 00:06:40.024
(audience cheer)

47
00:06:42.318 --> 00:06:44.654
(upbeat music)

48
00:06:46.155 --> 00:06:49.450
JENNIE (in Korean):
<i>I think those were really hectic moments.</i>

49
00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:50.785
<i>Because it was our first time.</i>

50
00:06:50.868 --> 00:06:53.663
I'm facing the stage right now,

51
00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:57.417
<i>and those were the seats for BLINKS.</i>

52
00:06:58.876 --> 00:07:03.840
There was a stage
that stretched out to the front,

53
00:07:04.549 --> 00:07:06.801
<i>and we ran underneath the stage.</i>

54
00:07:07.718 --> 00:07:09.679
<i>I think the most nervous moment is</i>

55
00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:14.225
<i>when we walk toward the backstage
with the anticipation of meeting our fans</i>

56
00:07:14.308 --> 00:07:18.396
<i>and performing for them.
I think that's the most nervous moment.</i>

57
00:07:18.479 --> 00:07:20.898
(audience cheer)

58
00:07:22.692 --> 00:07:25.903
(<i>Playing With Fire</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

59
00:08:02.857 --> 00:08:05.276
(<i>Playing With Fire</i> continues)

60
00:09:38.703 --> 00:09:41.706
(audience cheer)

61
00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:47.628
JENNIE (in English):
<i>You know, we haven't been able</i>

62
00:09:47.712 --> 00:09:50.506
<i>to perform live for a while now.</i>

63
00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:53.217
<i>And now that I think back at it...</i>

64
00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:59.682
performing on stage
is one of, one of the best parts.

65
00:10:00.349 --> 00:10:03.978
LISA (in Thai):
<i>I feel alive when I see our fans</i>

66
00:10:04.061 --> 00:10:08.691
<i>singing along to my song and enjoying it.</i>

67
00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:12.653
LISA (in Korean): <i>That feeling
of success like,</i><i>"Wow, I did it."</i>

68
00:10:12.737 --> 00:10:16.032
<i>"They're dancing together like I am!"</i>

69
00:10:16.115 --> 00:10:19.327
<i>When I feel that,
I think that's when I feel most alive.</i>

70
00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:21.495
ROSÉ (in English):
<i>It's upsetting that we can't</i>

71
00:10:21.579 --> 00:10:24.415
<i>have the fans watch the performance.</i>

72
00:10:24.498 --> 00:10:28.169
<i>Um, but I think
it just makes us more, like,</i>

73
00:10:28.919 --> 00:10:32.173
you know, gives us more space
to look forward to that day,

74
00:10:32.256 --> 00:10:36.302
and when that day comes for us,
we'll actually be in one room together.

75
00:10:36.385 --> 00:10:39.347
Um, that would be
a very, very special moment.

76
00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:41.432
(in Korean)
Wouldn't there be much to talk about

77
00:10:41.515 --> 00:10:43.225
when we meet? From now on?

78
00:10:43.309 --> 00:10:45.686
So I'm looking forward to it.

79
00:10:52.026 --> 00:10:53.402
BLACKPINK!

80
00:10:53.611 --> 00:10:55.488
(<i>How You Like That</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

81
00:11:01.077 --> 00:11:02.495
JISOO: The Show.

82
00:11:03.537 --> 00:11:05.581
(screaming)

83
00:11:13.422 --> 00:11:14.757
BLACKPINK!

84
00:11:22.264 --> 00:11:23.182
BLACKPINK!

85
00:11:23.599 --> 00:11:25.601
(quirky music)

86
00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:27.561
(all laugh)

87
00:11:27.645 --> 00:11:31.399
(indistinct chatter)

88
00:11:31.482 --> 00:11:35.319
(in Korean) Performing with the band
during the concert

89
00:11:35.403 --> 00:11:37.738
-is definitely really great.
-What's next?

90
00:11:37.822 --> 00:11:41.659
The energy is actually unreal.

91
00:11:41.742 --> 00:11:43.369
(laughs)

92
00:11:45.705 --> 00:11:48.124
All the instruments in the back,
singing live.

93
00:11:48.207 --> 00:11:51.669
But the production is
so much different too, so...

94
00:11:51.752 --> 00:11:54.130
Ahh. Yeah, yeah.

95
00:11:54.213 --> 00:11:59.385
I'm finally getting, "This is what
I was doing for two years," you know.

96
00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.806
(quirky music continues)

97
00:12:05.516 --> 00:12:07.017
How do we go in here?

98
00:12:08.936 --> 00:12:13.232
JISOO (in Korean): <i>We're doing our best
here so that BLINKs can also enjoy</i>

99
00:12:13.816 --> 00:12:19.321
<i>even the process of waiting
for our next performance.</i>

100
00:12:19.405 --> 00:12:20.573
<i>Please look forward to it!</i>

101
00:12:21.866 --> 00:12:23.701
(upbeat music)

102
00:12:31.959 --> 00:12:34.837
JENNIE (in Korean): <i>We worked really hard
to prepare for this concert,</i>

103
00:12:35.004 --> 00:12:37.882
so I hope you watch it
more than ten times.

104
00:12:39.592 --> 00:12:42.344
See you soon, bye.

105
00:12:46.557 --> 00:12:48.851
Let's go.

106
00:12:48.934 --> 00:12:50.227
Hello.

107
00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:55.399
(vocalizing)

108
00:12:55.483 --> 00:12:56.776
(laughs)

109
00:12:56.859 --> 00:12:58.778
ROSÉ: Hi, I'm here.

110
00:12:58.861 --> 00:13:00.529
What are we doing right now?

111
00:13:01.322 --> 00:13:02.990
-Emcee Girl.
-Emcee.

112
00:13:03.073 --> 00:13:03.949
-Okay.
-Yes.

113
00:13:04.074 --> 00:13:06.952
We got here today for the rehearsal.

114
00:13:07.036 --> 00:13:09.497
It's for tomorrow,
and what is this rehearsal for?

115
00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:12.166
I believe it's a rehearsal for The Show.

116
00:13:12.249 --> 00:13:15.002
(upbeat music)

117
00:13:24.553 --> 00:13:27.181
(<i>How You Like That</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

118
00:13:50.704 --> 00:13:54.416
JISOO (in Korean):
<i>I wanted to make it more perfect</i>

119
00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.710
<i>because I was not satisfied.</i>

120
00:13:56.794 --> 00:13:58.963
<i>It would've been great
if we had more time.</i>

121
00:14:01.674 --> 00:14:03.008
LISA (in Korean): <i>I'm so nervous.</i>

122
00:14:05.135 --> 00:14:07.555
(<i>How You Like That</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

123
00:14:13.769 --> 00:14:16.230
(audience cheer)

124
00:14:16.981 --> 00:14:19.817
(<i>Kill This Love</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

125
00:16:28.112 --> 00:16:30.948
(<i>Kill This Love</i> continues)

126
00:17:25.669 --> 00:17:28.005
(<i>Crazy Over You</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

127
00:18:21.642 --> 00:18:23.936
(<i>Crazy Over You</i> continues)

128
00:20:15.214 --> 00:20:17.257
(audience cheering)

129
00:20:23.764 --> 00:20:25.891
(<i>How You Like That</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

130
00:21:53.562 --> 00:21:56.023
(<i>How You Like That</i> continues)

131
00:23:16.311 --> 00:23:17.938
(audience cheering)

132
00:23:18.730 --> 00:23:20.273
(rattles)

133
00:23:26.238 --> 00:23:28.907
LISA (in Korean):
<i>It was the most fun I had in my life.</i>

134
00:23:29.491 --> 00:23:31.701
<i>And I had the best time of my life.</i>

135
00:23:32.953 --> 00:23:35.956
<i>Like for the rest of my life,
I think I'll continue to remember</i>

136
00:23:36.915 --> 00:23:38.875
<i>that moment, that feeling.</i>

137
00:23:41.086 --> 00:23:44.297
<i>A lot of things happened.
There were happy times,</i>

138
00:23:44.381 --> 00:23:46.383
<i>and there were sad times.</i>

139
00:23:46.466 --> 00:23:49.219
<i>I think those were the happiest times.</i>

140
00:23:50.679 --> 00:23:53.223
(upbeat music)

141
00:24:00.772 --> 00:24:03.442
<i>Oddly, when I try
to recollect difficult times,</i>

142
00:24:03.525 --> 00:24:06.445
<i>I can't seem to remember them.</i>

143
00:24:06.528 --> 00:24:07.654
(chuckles)

144
00:24:07.737 --> 00:24:12.367
<i>I just erase everything
that has to do with difficult times</i>

145
00:24:12.451 --> 00:24:13.994
<i>from my mind without realizing it.</i>

146
00:24:14.077 --> 00:24:17.247
LISA (in Thai): <i>I don't think
I'm overly positive or outgoing.</i>

147
00:24:17.330 --> 00:24:19.583
<i>I am a normal person
just like everyone else.</i>

148
00:24:19.666 --> 00:24:21.626
<i>Every day I'm like this.</i>

149
00:24:21.710 --> 00:24:23.795
(in English)
<i>Every day, I'm like this.</i>

150
00:24:23.879 --> 00:24:24.963
(finger snaps)

151
00:24:27.299 --> 00:24:29.718
(upbeat music)

152
00:24:33.263 --> 00:24:38.351
LISA (in Thai): <i>I knew what I wanted to do
since I was young.</i>

153
00:24:38.435 --> 00:24:42.022
<i>I believe I am a very lucky person.</i>

154
00:24:42.564 --> 00:24:46.276
<i>I had a clear goal
to become a superstar in the future.</i>

155
00:24:46.359 --> 00:24:49.613
<i>I worked hard to make my dream come true.</i>

156
00:24:50.906 --> 00:24:53.116
(upbeat music continues)

157
00:25:00.874 --> 00:25:03.502
<i>I try to think that I am happy,</i>

158
00:25:04.211 --> 00:25:08.507
<i>without having to stress out too much.</i>

159
00:25:08.590 --> 00:25:12.928
<i>I hope others could also think like that.</i>

160
00:25:14.763 --> 00:25:16.264
(in English)
<i>Life is super short.</i>

161
00:25:19.434 --> 00:25:21.645
(<i>Don't Know What To Do</i>
by BLACKPINK playing)

162
00:26:52.193 --> 00:26:54.738
(<i>Don't Know What To Do</i> continues)

163
00:28:36.297 --> 00:28:38.717
(audience cheer)

164
00:28:41.010 --> 00:28:43.430
(<i>Lovesick Girls</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

165
00:29:51.623 --> 00:29:54.584
(<i>Lovesick Girls</i> continues)

166
00:31:51.200 --> 00:31:54.370
(audience cheer)

167
00:31:58.750 --> 00:32:00.793
(<i>Pretty Savage</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

168
00:33:13.866 --> 00:33:15.952
(audience cheer)

169
00:33:16.035 --> 00:33:18.037
(<i>Pretty Savage</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

170
00:33:22.875 --> 00:33:24.794
(drumbeats)

171
00:34:04.542 --> 00:34:06.586
(<i>Pretty Savage</i> continues)

172
00:35:45.768 --> 00:35:48.187
(<i>Pretty Savage</i> continues)

173
00:36:33.316 --> 00:36:35.359
(audience cheering)

174
00:36:35.443 --> 00:36:37.153
(rattles)

175
00:36:43.451 --> 00:36:45.703
(<i>You Never Know</i> by BLACKPINK)

176
00:36:58.966 --> 00:37:03.554
JISOO (in Korean): <i>I guess I thought that
I am a lot stronger than I believed.</i>

177
00:37:06.307 --> 00:37:09.852
<i>There are times when I feel hurt</i>

178
00:37:10.311 --> 00:37:13.606
<i>or when I go through hardships,</i>

179
00:37:13.689 --> 00:37:16.442
<i>but my way of overcoming those times is</i>

180
00:37:16.525 --> 00:37:19.487
<i>preparing more for what's to come</i>

181
00:37:19.570 --> 00:37:21.948
<i>or focusing on thinking about
how I can better move forward.</i>

182
00:37:23.950 --> 00:37:26.369
(upbeat music)

183
00:37:51.769 --> 00:37:53.104
<i>Attitude towards life?</i>

184
00:37:56.524 --> 00:37:58.192
<i>That's a hard one.</i>
(laughs)

185
00:37:59.110 --> 00:38:00.778
<i>Well...</i>

186
00:38:02.738 --> 00:38:06.033
<i>I think I just live my life
enjoying every moment.</i>

187
00:38:18.379 --> 00:38:20.381
(telephone ringing)

188
00:38:22.758 --> 00:38:24.885
(upbeat music)

189
00:38:36.856 --> 00:38:42.570
<i>What I felt throughout the process
is that if I think too far ahead</i>

190
00:38:43.154 --> 00:38:45.156
<i>about the things that hasn't happened yet.</i>

191
00:38:45.239 --> 00:38:46.907
<i>I could also get anxious
and worry about it,</i>

192
00:38:46.991 --> 00:38:48.951
<i>then end up missing many things.</i>

193
00:38:49.035 --> 00:38:51.787
<i>So I try to live in the moment</i>

194
00:38:51.871 --> 00:38:56.000
<i>and try to have fun, I think.</i>

195
00:38:58.961 --> 00:39:01.005
(upbeat music)

196
00:39:08.387 --> 00:39:10.056
LISA: Oh, yes!

197
00:39:10.431 --> 00:39:13.642
JISOO (in Korean):
<i>It's almost time to meet all the BLINKs</i>

198
00:39:13.726 --> 00:39:16.771
<i>from all over the world</i>
<i>who have waited so long.</i>

199
00:39:16.854 --> 00:39:18.105
<i>I am very nervous,</i>

200
00:39:18.189 --> 00:39:21.650
<i>and since you've waited so much,
I am going to show you the best.</i>

201
00:39:22.026 --> 00:39:25.488
<i>Show us a lot of support and enjoy it.</i>

202
00:39:29.742 --> 00:39:32.203
(<i>Playing With Fire</i> instrumental)

203
00:39:36.791 --> 00:39:40.378
Thailand is also Lisa's hometown,

204
00:39:40.461 --> 00:39:46.300
so I think it's more meaningful to start
our world tour in Lisa's hometown.

205
00:39:46.384 --> 00:39:51.555
Starting from Thailand,
we're going to North America

206
00:39:51.639 --> 00:39:55.559
and Europe
to meet BLINKs around the world.

207
00:39:55.643 --> 00:39:58.437
I'm so honored and looking forward to it.

208
00:39:58.521 --> 00:40:01.482
-(all applause)
-(indistinct speech)

209
00:40:05.736 --> 00:40:08.114
JENNIE (in Korean):
<i>The phrase "BLACKPINK's world tour"</i>

210
00:40:08.197 --> 00:40:11.200
<i>still feels very foreign to me.</i>

211
00:40:11.283 --> 00:40:14.245
I still can't believe it.
(chuckles)

212
00:40:18.416 --> 00:40:22.628
I prepared lots of fun stuff
for our concert

213
00:40:23.129 --> 00:40:26.590
and want to do more exciting things
in different countries.

214
00:40:26.674 --> 00:40:28.968
That's how I feel.

215
00:40:29.051 --> 00:40:34.140
I hope many BLINKs around the world come.
It's gonna be fun.

216
00:40:34.765 --> 00:40:37.643
(upbeat music)

217
00:40:42.148 --> 00:40:44.358
(audience cheering)

218
00:40:48.612 --> 00:40:50.156
What's up, Bangkok!

219
00:40:50.239 --> 00:40:52.450
(audience cheering)

220
00:40:53.033 --> 00:40:55.619
(<i>As If It's Your Last</i>
by BLACKPINK playing)

221
00:41:24.940 --> 00:41:26.984
(in Thai)
It was very touching.

222
00:41:27.067 --> 00:41:31.280
I think I'm very lucky to see them,
I could really tell how hard they tried,

223
00:41:31.363 --> 00:41:36.827
<i>from the beginning to the end.
I hope they take care of themselves.</i>

224
00:41:36.911 --> 00:41:40.748
I hope everyone stays healthy

225
00:41:40.831 --> 00:41:44.960
<i>because they have to go perform
all around the world.</i>

226
00:41:45.461 --> 00:41:47.588
(<i>As If It's Your Last</i>
by BLACKPINK playing)

227
00:42:03.812 --> 00:42:08.108
LISA (in Korean): <i>We're going to visit
BLINKs in other countries too,</i>

228
00:42:08.192 --> 00:42:10.361
<i>so please wait a little more.</i>

229
00:42:10.444 --> 00:42:14.031
We'll be there very soon,
and we'll show you a great performance.

230
00:42:14.114 --> 00:42:15.991
Wait a little, BLINKs.

231
00:42:19.453 --> 00:42:23.958
(in English) Welcome to the BLACKPINK
2019 World Tour In Your Area, Jakarta!

232
00:42:24.041 --> 00:42:25.584
-Hong Kong!
-Manila!

233
00:42:25.668 --> 00:42:27.211
-Singapore!
-Macau!

234
00:42:27.294 --> 00:42:29.255
-Kuala Lumpur!
-Taipei!

235
00:42:29.338 --> 00:42:31.382
(audience cheering)

236
00:42:31.966 --> 00:42:33.884
(<i>Forever Young</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

237
00:42:51.735 --> 00:42:56.073
Most amazing humans that I have ever seen.
Like, I love them so much.

238
00:42:58.409 --> 00:43:00.119
Our BLACKPINK has their own swag.

239
00:43:01.829 --> 00:43:03.789
(<i>Forever Young</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

240
00:43:07.334 --> 00:43:09.920
FANS: BLACKPINK! Welcome to LA!

241
00:43:10.004 --> 00:43:11.213
Welcome to Texas!

242
00:43:11.297 --> 00:43:13.716
-Welcome to Atlanta!
-Welcome to Canada!

243
00:43:13.799 --> 00:43:15.342
Welcome to Fort Worth!

244
00:43:15.426 --> 00:43:18.512
Welcome to Newark, BLACKPINK!

245
00:43:18.596 --> 00:43:21.432
(audience cheering)

246
00:43:21.515 --> 00:43:23.892
(<i>Ddu-Du Ddu-Du</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

247
00:43:44.913 --> 00:43:46.915
(audience cheering)

248
00:43:49.543 --> 00:43:54.923
I just love seeing
how four young women are being themselves.

249
00:43:55.007 --> 00:43:56.925
They are like role models to us.

250
00:43:57.009 --> 00:43:59.386
-Yeah, we all want to be like BLACKPINK.
-Yeah.

251
00:43:59.470 --> 00:44:01.972
(<i>Kill This Love</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

252
00:44:37.174 --> 00:44:39.385
Hi, Melbourne, I'm Rosé.

253
00:44:39.468 --> 00:44:41.095
(audience cheer)

254
00:44:41.220 --> 00:44:43.597
(<i>Kick It</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

255
00:44:59.488 --> 00:45:01.740
(<i>Kick It</i> continues)

256
00:45:13.877 --> 00:45:15.754
(in Thai)
Hello, I'm Lisa.

257
00:45:15.838 --> 00:45:16.880
(audience cheer)

258
00:45:16.964 --> 00:45:19.758
(in English)
I'm so happy to be back here in Thailand.

259
00:45:20.551 --> 00:45:23.512
(audience cheer)

260
00:45:24.763 --> 00:45:27.349
ROSÉ (in English): All four of us,
we did really, really well,

261
00:45:27.433 --> 00:45:30.561
and I'm very proud
of each and every one of us,

262
00:45:30.644 --> 00:45:32.271
cause we went through a lot.

263
00:45:32.771 --> 00:45:33.772
(laughs)

264
00:45:33.856 --> 00:45:39.236
Like, I know you guys only see the stuff
that's on stage, but I feel like

265
00:45:39.319 --> 00:45:42.281
we all go through so much,
and I am very, very proud...

266
00:45:42.364 --> 00:45:43.323
Now I'm going to cry.

267
00:45:43.407 --> 00:45:45.784
Everybody stop crying.

268
00:45:46.785 --> 00:45:49.705
-Everyone's crying.
-Everyone's crying.

269
00:45:49.955 --> 00:45:51.206
Aww.

270
00:45:54.918 --> 00:45:58.380
(in Thai)
I'm a little shy,

271
00:45:58.464 --> 00:46:02.551
but I want to tell everyone...

272
00:46:02.634 --> 00:46:03.635
Huh.

273
00:46:03.719 --> 00:46:06.096
(in English) Thank you again
so much, BLINKs. We love you.

274
00:46:06.180 --> 00:46:07.347
(in Thai)
Thank you so much.

275
00:46:07.431 --> 00:46:11.018
(in English) We love you guys so much,
and we have so much more coming.

276
00:46:11.101 --> 00:46:12.561
This is just the beginning for us.

277
00:46:12.644 --> 00:46:14.521
(audience cheer)

278
00:46:14.605 --> 00:46:18.150
We always love you guys. Thank you.

279
00:46:18.233 --> 00:46:20.652
(audience cheer)

280
00:46:25.240 --> 00:46:27.117
(rattles)

281
00:46:30.412 --> 00:46:31.413
ROSÉ: <i>Pure...</i>

282
00:46:33.499 --> 00:46:34.958
<i>Poetic...</i>

283
00:46:36.251 --> 00:46:38.086
<i>Utmost Passionate...</i>

284
00:46:39.755 --> 00:46:41.215
<i>Never Dying...</i>

285
00:46:43.217 --> 00:46:44.551
<i>Tangible...</i>

286
00:46:45.844 --> 00:46:47.471
<i>Forever young...</i>

287
00:46:49.431 --> 00:46:50.724
<i>Unselfish...</i>

288
00:46:52.351 --> 00:46:54.478
<i>You and me...</i>

289
00:46:54.561 --> 00:46:56.563
<i>Desire...</i>

290
00:46:59.983 --> 00:47:02.694
(barking)

291
00:47:05.072 --> 00:47:06.907
ROSÉ: <i>When you're growing up,
you just feel like</i>

292
00:47:06.990 --> 00:47:11.036
<i>there are no limits</i>
<i>to your goals and dreams.</i>

293
00:47:11.912 --> 00:47:13.539
<i>I've had a very hard time here and there,</i>

294
00:47:13.622 --> 00:47:17.668
<i>because it was quite challenging
as a 16-year-old,</i>

295
00:47:18.210 --> 00:47:20.546
<i>growing up in a whole different culture.</i>

296
00:47:21.672 --> 00:47:24.132
<i>It didn't seem realistic at the time,</i>

297
00:47:24.216 --> 00:47:27.052
<i>but I just knew that</i>
<i>I would make it come true.</i>

298
00:47:28.428 --> 00:47:32.099
<i>I actually envy myself as a trainee</i>

299
00:47:32.182 --> 00:47:36.186
<i>because I do believe</i>
<i>that I was very strong-willed,</i>

300
00:47:36.270 --> 00:47:38.730
<i>very stubborn, so sure about my future</i>

301
00:47:38.814 --> 00:47:41.441
<i>and so determined to reach my goals,</i>

302
00:47:41.525 --> 00:47:43.777
<i>and I knew I would get there</i>
<i>for some reason.</i>

303
00:47:47.322 --> 00:47:52.536
<i>I always have to think back on
how passionate I was towards music</i>

304
00:47:52.619 --> 00:47:53.787
<i>and how much music,</i>

305
00:47:54.121 --> 00:47:56.832
<i>uh, gave me a lot of the part.</i>

306
00:47:56.915 --> 00:48:00.502
<i>And it turned out to become my life now,</i>

307
00:48:00.586 --> 00:48:02.588
<i>um, to the current day too, so...</i>

308
00:48:02.671 --> 00:48:04.506
<i>Yeah, music is a big part.</i>

309
00:48:04.590 --> 00:48:07.426
(<i>On The Ground</i> instrumental)

310
00:48:07.509 --> 00:48:10.971
<i>Preparing for music in itself
is always a personal thing.</i>

311
00:48:11.597 --> 00:48:14.349
<i>Being able to explore for the first time</i>

312
00:48:14.433 --> 00:48:19.021
<i>what my music will be about,</i>
<i>and what I'm gonna be showing my fans is</i>

313
00:48:19.104 --> 00:48:21.315
<i>a very rewarding experience.</i>

314
00:48:23.442 --> 00:48:26.862
<i>During the preparations for The Show,</i>

315
00:48:26.945 --> 00:48:30.908
<i>I think I was also preparing
my solo project</i>

316
00:48:30.991 --> 00:48:35.913
<i>I had just finished
the last shoot for</i> Gone,

317
00:48:35.996 --> 00:48:38.749
<i>so that was the second music video</i>
<i>I did back-to-back.</i>

318
00:48:39.207 --> 00:48:42.628
<i>To be honest, I think it's the first time
I'm actually saying this out loud</i>

319
00:48:42.711 --> 00:48:45.589
<i>that it really was a challenge.
But at the same time,</i>

320
00:48:45.672 --> 00:48:49.343
<i>I was very, very grateful</i>
<i>for the opportunities that I was given.</i>

321
00:48:49.843 --> 00:48:54.890
<i>It was a lot of fun creating, thinking,
and just making all things come to life,</i>

322
00:48:54.973 --> 00:48:56.808
<i>all of my, our ideas.</i>

323
00:48:57.517 --> 00:48:59.227
<i>I think I tried my best.</i>

324
00:48:59.645 --> 00:49:01.688
<i>I don't think I would go back</i>
<i>and change anything,</i>

325
00:49:01.772 --> 00:49:05.150
<i>because I really did try</i>
<i>to pour my heart and soul into it.</i>

326
00:49:07.069 --> 00:49:09.696
(<i>Gone</i> by Rosé playing)

327
00:50:05.752 --> 00:50:08.046
(<i>Gone</i> continues)

328
00:50:42.956 --> 00:50:44.833
(audience cheering)

329
00:50:45.542 --> 00:50:48.170
(<i>Love To Hate Me</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

330
00:51:45.352 --> 00:51:47.813
(<i>Love To Hate Me</i> continues)

331
00:53:07.851 --> 00:53:10.478
(<i>You Never Know</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

332
00:54:00.862 --> 00:54:03.531
(<i>You Never Know</i> continues)

333
00:56:56.454 --> 00:56:59.290
(audience cheer)

334
00:57:01.709 --> 00:57:03.294
(rattles)

335
00:57:11.136 --> 00:57:14.431
JENNIE (in English):
<i>I feel like as far as I remember</i>

336
00:57:14.514 --> 00:57:17.851
<i>ever since I was a kid,
I've always been the shy kid.</i>

337
00:57:19.227 --> 00:57:23.189
<i>I didn't really like
talking in front of a lot of people.</i>

338
00:57:24.816 --> 00:57:28.486
<i>I have a strive
on searching for something new inside</i>

339
00:57:28.570 --> 00:57:32.407
<i>where I want to develop that
into something of my own,</i>

340
00:57:32.866 --> 00:57:36.953
<i>and create something
that hasn't been out to the world.</i>

341
00:57:38.913 --> 00:57:43.668
<i>But when it comes to performing on stage,</i>

342
00:57:44.461 --> 00:57:49.257
<i>I think I put on this entire new self,</i>

343
00:57:49.340 --> 00:57:51.509
<i>where I'm not afraid.</i>

344
00:57:51.593 --> 00:57:53.553
(<i>Solo</i> by Jennie playing)

345
00:57:57.474 --> 00:58:00.185
<i>When I'm performing,</i>
<i>I forget about everything.</i>

346
00:58:00.560 --> 00:58:02.520
<i>It's just all about me,</i>

347
00:58:02.937 --> 00:58:06.274
<i>expressing myself, expressing our music.</i>

348
00:58:06.858 --> 00:58:10.612
<i>I guess I do have a switch inside
somewhere where I turn it on and off,</i>

349
00:58:10.695 --> 00:58:13.573
<i>but it's not something
that I do purposely.</i>

350
00:58:13.656 --> 00:58:15.742
<i>I think it reacts with music.</i>

351
00:58:16.034 --> 00:58:22.123
<i>And the very first energy that I meet
whenever I first jump up on the stage.</i>

352
00:58:23.833 --> 00:58:26.211
(upbeat music)

353
00:58:43.603 --> 00:58:46.564
JENNIE: <i>I wanna say it's just something
that I was born with,</i>

354
00:58:46.648 --> 00:58:49.400
<i>because I'm proud of it,
and I'm happy doing it.</i>

355
00:58:50.360 --> 00:58:51.486
<i>So, yeah.</i>

356
00:58:57.784 --> 00:59:00.161
(<i>Solo</i> by Jennie playing)

357
01:00:32.670 --> 01:00:34.922
(<i>Solo</i> continues)

358
01:01:40.780 --> 01:01:43.199
(audience cheer)

359
01:01:48.413 --> 01:01:52.250
JENNIE (in Korean):
<i>I think our identity is rather fixed.</i>

360
01:01:52.750 --> 01:01:54.627
<i>I like to think that</i>

361
01:01:54.711 --> 01:01:58.297
<i>we have a lot of pride
in having both colors, black and pink.</i>

362
01:01:58.381 --> 01:01:59.841
But because of that,

363
01:01:59.924 --> 01:02:03.970
we're still in the process
of continuously experimenting.

364
01:02:04.053 --> 01:02:07.724
<i>And fortunately, rather than
not being able to predict it,</i>

365
01:02:07.807 --> 01:02:11.978
<i>we continue to go forward
in the direction that we want.</i>

366
01:02:12.061 --> 01:02:15.398
I just enjoy the whole process.

367
01:02:15.481 --> 01:02:17.066
JISOO (in Korean):
<i>We all grew up in different cultures.</i>

368
01:02:17.150 --> 01:02:19.569
<i>These various cultures overlapped,
and a group was born.</i>

369
01:02:20.611 --> 01:02:22.613
But instead of forcing them into one,

370
01:02:22.697 --> 01:02:26.367
we worked as a group

371
01:02:26.451 --> 01:02:28.828
without losing each of our individuality.

372
01:02:28.911 --> 01:02:33.583
I think that rather emerged
as the color of the group BLACKPINK.

373
01:02:34.500 --> 01:02:38.838
I think we shine the brightest

374
01:02:38.921 --> 01:02:41.132
when we do what we love to do.

375
01:02:41.215 --> 01:02:43.676
Now that'd be music, right?

376
01:02:43.760 --> 01:02:48.639
When we are fully expressing
what we want to express,

377
01:02:49.265 --> 01:02:52.435
-that's when we shine the brightest.
-(all laugh)

378
01:02:52.518 --> 01:02:55.897
ROSÉ (in Korean):
<i>So I think it'd be great for us to show</i>

379
01:02:55.980 --> 01:03:00.359
a lot of things
that we enjoy doing in the future.

380
01:03:00.443 --> 01:03:03.529
JISOO (in Korean) <i>As we do this,
we've always done everything thinking,</i>

381
01:03:03.613 --> 01:03:08.242
<i>"We could show something like this.
This time, we can show this."</i>

382
01:03:08.868 --> 01:03:12.872
<i>I think we can continue
to show different sides of us.</i>

383
01:03:13.748 --> 01:03:18.878
We plan on continuing to do
what we want and show it.

384
01:03:23.257 --> 01:03:27.887
Five years is not too short
and not too long of a time, right?

385
01:03:28.429 --> 01:03:32.350
<i>But a lot of different things happened.</i>

386
01:03:32.934 --> 01:03:35.937
<i>There were happy times, and sad times.</i>

387
01:03:36.729 --> 01:03:43.736
<i>I think those were
the happiest times of my 20s.</i>

388
01:03:46.781 --> 01:03:50.034
ROSÉ (in Korean):
<i>When we were on the tour,</i>

389
01:03:50.117 --> 01:03:54.121
<i>I'd always feel hectic thinking about</i>

390
01:03:54.205 --> 01:03:57.500
<i>which city we have to go next and such.</i>

391
01:03:58.084 --> 01:04:02.338
But after seeing this video,
I could see that we laughed a lot

392
01:04:02.421 --> 01:04:07.426
<i>and really enjoyed our time together.</i>

393
01:04:09.136 --> 01:04:13.933
When we first debuted,
we faced all kinds of experiences.

394
01:04:14.433 --> 01:04:17.895
<i>Back then, there was a fear
about whether or not we were doing well,</i>

395
01:04:17.979 --> 01:04:21.440
<i>feeling uncertain about some things.</i>

396
01:04:22.066 --> 01:04:24.193
JENNIE (in Korean):
<i>When we had our first concert,</i>

397
01:04:24.944 --> 01:04:30.950
what we say on stage is also
a very important part of our concert.

398
01:04:31.033 --> 01:04:35.955
I was really nervous, like,
"Let's not make any mistake."

399
01:04:36.163 --> 01:04:40.835
It's already been a little over two years
since we debuted.

400
01:04:40.918 --> 01:04:44.881
And to be able to have a concert

401
01:04:44.964 --> 01:04:49.677
at such a big venue in Korea
in Seoul like this...

402
01:04:49.760 --> 01:04:54.015
Even as I'm saying it,
I feel like we've improved very much.

403
01:04:54.098 --> 01:04:57.435
And it was all possible thanks to BLINKs.
Right, everyone?

404
01:04:57.518 --> 01:05:00.771
We've been together since day one.

405
01:05:00.855 --> 01:05:05.651
I like to think we've grown a little bit
seeing how we've become more comfortable

406
01:05:05.735 --> 01:05:09.113
with making a speech
and looking after one another

407
01:05:09.196 --> 01:05:10.489
<i>when we're on stage.</i>

408
01:05:10.573 --> 01:05:13.784
ROSÉ (in Korean): <i>I like to believe that</i>

409
01:05:13.868 --> 01:05:16.662
we still have that energy
from when we were trainees.

410
01:05:16.746 --> 01:05:18.456
(all laugh)

411
01:05:18.539 --> 01:05:22.001
I'm so moved,
thank you all so much for coming.

412
01:05:22.585 --> 01:05:24.921
JISOO (in Korean):
<i>Since the four of us are in this together,</i>

413
01:05:25.004 --> 01:05:26.464
<i>we decided to have a talk</i>

414
01:05:26.547 --> 01:05:31.427
<i>on trusting each other more
and trying to enjoy everything.</i>

415
01:05:31.510 --> 01:05:35.431
Since then, it became more enjoyable
to take on new challenges,

416
01:05:35.514 --> 01:05:39.101
we became more excited,
and began to look forward to things.

417
01:05:39.185 --> 01:05:41.395
I think we grew up a little.

418
01:05:41.479 --> 01:05:47.652
We are always here for you, BLINKs,
so please stay with us too. Thank you!

419
01:05:47.735 --> 01:05:48.653
(audience cheer)

420
01:05:48.736 --> 01:05:50.237
When the four of us are together,

421
01:05:50.321 --> 01:05:55.076
we always laugh and talk
just like we did when we were trainees.

422
01:05:55.159 --> 01:05:57.912
It's just so fun to work together too.

423
01:05:57.995 --> 01:06:00.164
-I think we're the same.
-We are the same.

424
01:06:01.123 --> 01:06:03.542
Now we don't even have to say a word.

425
01:06:03.626 --> 01:06:06.462
We just look
at each other's eyes and know.

426
01:06:06.545 --> 01:06:08.547
-(all laugh)
-We just know.

427
01:06:08.631 --> 01:06:10.091
Tell us, Lisa.

428
01:06:10.174 --> 01:06:14.512
Yes. Thanks to all of your support

429
01:06:14.845 --> 01:06:19.141
and love, I will strive to work harder

430
01:06:19.225 --> 01:06:21.477
as Lisa of BLACKPINK, everyone.

431
01:06:21.560 --> 01:06:22.979
I love you, BLINKs.

432
01:06:23.062 --> 01:06:25.314
(audience cheer)

433
01:06:27.858 --> 01:06:30.486
(<i>Whistle</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

434
01:07:10.943 --> 01:07:13.279
(<i>Whistle</i> continues)

435
01:09:57.067 --> 01:09:59.695
(audience cheer)

436
01:10:07.536 --> 01:10:10.122
(<i>As If It's Your Last</i>
by BLACKPINK playing)

437
01:10:57.836 --> 01:11:00.005
(<i>As If It's Your Last</i> continues)

438
01:13:34.660 --> 01:13:37.287
(audience cheer)

439
01:13:42.418 --> 01:13:45.045
(<i>Boombayah</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

440
01:14:28.297 --> 01:14:30.549
(<i>Boombayah</i> continues)

441
01:16:10.315 --> 01:16:11.858
JENNIE: Everybody dance!

442
01:16:27.916 --> 01:16:30.544
(audience cheer)

443
01:16:42.222 --> 01:16:43.932
LISA (in Korean): BLINKs.

444
01:16:44.641 --> 01:16:50.063
We just finished the last US show. Yay!

445
01:16:50.564 --> 01:16:52.608
Wow, I still can't hear anything.

446
01:16:52.691 --> 01:16:53.859
(vocalizing)

447
01:16:53.942 --> 01:16:55.235
Is my voice coming out all right?

448
01:16:55.319 --> 01:16:58.447
I'm so sad it's already over.

449
01:16:58.530 --> 01:17:04.870
I'm sad to see it come to an end.
It feels bittersweet.

450
01:17:05.162 --> 01:17:08.248
Over the past month and a half,

451
01:17:09.041 --> 01:17:13.670
there were
many new and exciting experiences.

452
01:17:13.754 --> 01:17:18.925
Still, I had a lot of time
to relax in different cities.

453
01:17:20.886 --> 01:17:22.471
It was great.

454
01:17:23.555 --> 01:17:27.976
JISOO (in Korean): <i>We performed a lot,
and it was a meaningful time.</i>

455
01:17:28.477 --> 01:17:32.773
ROSÉ (in Korean): <i>I think I enjoyed
every moment more than I thought I would.</i>

456
01:17:32.856 --> 01:17:36.026
<i>It was a meaningful tour,
like a surprise gift.</i>

457
01:17:36.693 --> 01:17:39.821
JENNIE (in Korean): <i>What I felt the most
during the tour was...</i>

458
01:17:40.447 --> 01:17:41.698
<i>Uh...</i>

459
01:17:42.282 --> 01:17:45.619
<i>It really was a time for me</i>

460
01:17:45.702 --> 01:17:49.289
<i>to rethink of myself
as a member of BLACKPINK.</i>

461
01:17:49.373 --> 01:17:51.583
(light music)

462
01:17:57.506 --> 01:18:02.886
I honestly don't think we've changed much
just because it's been five years.

463
01:18:02.969 --> 01:18:05.472
<i>We haven't changed much,</i>

464
01:18:05.555 --> 01:18:08.642
<i>but what's more reassuring is
having fans by our side,</i>

465
01:18:08.725 --> 01:18:12.270
<i>who have always supported us
for the last five years.</i>

466
01:18:12.354 --> 01:18:15.315
There will be the sixth
and the seventh anniversary in the future,

467
01:18:15.399 --> 01:18:21.029
and it feels like
we're getting stronger over the years.

468
01:18:21.113 --> 01:18:25.826
I really like the feeling of us and BLINKs

469
01:18:25.909 --> 01:18:27.953
becoming a lot closer.

470
01:18:28.870 --> 01:18:32.374
(in English) I can't believe
it's already been five years. Um...

471
01:18:33.291 --> 01:18:39.214
I wish this movie gets
a little bit of our BLINKs'

472
01:18:40.424 --> 01:18:43.176
frustration out, and...

473
01:18:44.386 --> 01:18:47.597
it's a good memory
that we are also gonna have.

474
01:18:47.681 --> 01:18:50.976
And we can look back at it next year
and talk about it, maybe?

475
01:18:51.768 --> 01:18:54.771
It's a new step for us,
I'm really glad that

476
01:18:55.689 --> 01:18:57.774
we got this opportunity.

477
01:18:59.276 --> 01:19:01.194
And I miss you guys.

478
01:19:02.446 --> 01:19:04.865
(audience singing)

479
01:19:27.512 --> 01:19:32.392
LISA (in Korean): <i>I feel like
I cried a lot over the five years.</i>

480
01:19:32.476 --> 01:19:37.314
<i>When I watch the videos
from my fans, I tear up.</i>

481
01:19:37.397 --> 01:19:41.318
I was so touched
when I just saw that video.

482
01:19:41.401 --> 01:19:44.988
Even now as I'm talking,
I feel like I'm going to cry.

483
01:19:45.071 --> 01:19:49.659
Because those were such happy times.

484
01:19:49.743 --> 01:19:52.370
(audience singing)

485
01:19:56.082 --> 01:19:58.502
(audience cheer)

486
01:20:02.380 --> 01:20:06.301
ROSÉ (in Korean): <i>Five years ago,
we were five years younger,</i>

487
01:20:06.384 --> 01:20:09.179
and it was probably the same
with our BLINKs.

488
01:20:09.262 --> 01:20:11.264
As we continued to grow,

489
01:20:11.348 --> 01:20:15.393
I was very happy to be able
to share that time with BLINKs.

490
01:20:15.477 --> 01:20:19.773
<i>I miss them so much
since we haven't been able to meet lately.</i>

491
01:20:19.856 --> 01:20:23.735
<i>But because we missed each other so much,
when we meet again,</i>

492
01:20:23.819 --> 01:20:26.029
<i>I'm so excited at the thought</i>

493
01:20:26.112 --> 01:20:30.075
<i>that we'll be able to greet them
with the biggest joy.</i>

494
01:20:30.158 --> 01:20:32.160
<i>Thank you so much
for always worrying about us,</i>

495
01:20:32.244 --> 01:20:36.039
and above all, thank you that
you always show us love and support.

496
01:20:36.122 --> 01:20:38.166
We miss you so much.

497
01:20:38.250 --> 01:20:42.295
JENNIE (in Korean):
<i>BLINKs have always been there by our side</i>

498
01:20:42.379 --> 01:20:44.673
no matter which year of our career it is,

499
01:20:44.756 --> 01:20:48.635
showing us so much unchanging love.

500
01:20:49.052 --> 01:20:53.431
That's what makes us
want to move forward further.

501
01:20:53.515 --> 01:20:58.311
I hope you stay
with BLACKPINK all the way,

502
01:20:58.395 --> 01:21:02.065
as if we are lifelong companions.

503
01:21:02.148 --> 01:21:04.901
Thank you, and love you always.

504
01:21:04.985 --> 01:21:05.986
(soft chuckle)

505
01:21:07.404 --> 01:21:13.493
Whenever we talk about how we feel inside,

506
01:21:13.577 --> 01:21:15.161
I always have nothing to say.

507
01:21:15.245 --> 01:21:17.372
I feel very shy about it, but...

508
01:21:29.551 --> 01:21:31.595
What should I say? Hm...

509
01:21:35.974 --> 01:21:40.270
There are so many things
that I wanted to say, but...

510
01:21:40.353 --> 01:21:41.438
(sniffs)

511
01:21:41.521 --> 01:21:44.900
To keep it short...

512
01:21:48.653 --> 01:21:51.156
(in Thai)
Thank you so much.

513
01:21:51.239 --> 01:21:57.871
Thank you so much for loving me,
as me, as Lisa of BLACKPINK.

514
01:21:57.954 --> 01:22:00.916
When I was a kid, I never imagined...

515
01:22:00.999 --> 01:22:02.042
(sniffs)

516
01:22:02.542 --> 01:22:05.211
...I could be loved

517
01:22:06.379 --> 01:22:12.469
by people all over the world.

518
01:22:12.552 --> 01:22:13.595
(sniffles)

519
01:22:13.678 --> 01:22:17.724
(in English) Honestly,
thank you for always supporting me.

520
01:22:19.059 --> 01:22:20.393
Yeah, that's all.

521
01:22:21.394 --> 01:22:27.984
(in Thai) I don't know how to describe
my feelings other than saying thank you.

522
01:22:31.571 --> 01:22:32.405
(in English)
Thank you, BLACKPINK

523
01:22:32.489 --> 01:22:35.533
for showing us that
we can do everything, what we love,

524
01:22:35.617 --> 01:22:37.160
when we really believe in it.

525
01:22:37.243 --> 01:22:38.370
We love you.

526
01:22:38.453 --> 01:22:43.249
Keep going hard, ladies.
We got you. We ride or die. We love you.

527
01:22:43.333 --> 01:22:47.545
I will forever support BLACKPINK,
and thank you for everything.

528
01:22:48.046 --> 01:22:49.130
Me too.

529
01:22:50.090 --> 01:22:52.133
-You're a queen.
-We love you.

530
01:22:52.217 --> 01:22:54.678
I love you guys,
and you guys are doing so well.

531
01:22:54.761 --> 01:22:56.346
And I hope to get to see you again.

532
01:22:59.099 --> 01:23:01.267
(<i>You Never Know</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

533
01:23:24.833 --> 01:23:27.502
JENNIE (in Korean):
<i>As we go up on the stage like this,</i>

534
01:23:27.585 --> 01:23:32.507
<i>we can see our light sticks shaking
and hear the cheering.</i>

535
01:23:34.676 --> 01:23:36.678
<i>It's so pretty.</i>

536
01:23:37.679 --> 01:23:40.849
LISA (in Korean):
<i>Some people set it so that it beeps.</i>

537
01:23:40.932 --> 01:23:42.976
<i>You can set it like that.</i>

538
01:23:43.059 --> 01:23:47.647
<i>Every time I hear it, I get so excited.
It's so encouraging.</i>

539
01:23:50.900 --> 01:23:54.779
-BLACKPINK!
-BLACKPINK!

540
01:23:54.988 --> 01:24:00.994
-BLACKPINK!
-BLACKPINK!

541
01:24:01.077 --> 01:24:04.289
We'll cherish this truly precious memory.

542
01:24:04.372 --> 01:24:08.251
Thanks to all of you supporting
and loving us wholeheartedly.

543
01:24:08.585 --> 01:24:13.298
We'll keep this memory
and strive to grow further as BLACKPINK.

544
01:24:13.381 --> 01:24:14.716
Thank you.

545
01:24:14.799 --> 01:24:16.468
(audience cheer)

546
01:24:16.551 --> 01:24:18.970
(<i>You Never know</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

547
01:24:28.354 --> 01:24:30.315
(in English)
Stay with us, BLINKs.

548
01:24:33.777 --> 01:24:35.111
JENNIE (in Korean): <i>Just once more,</i>

549
01:24:35.195 --> 01:24:36.905
<i>we'll see you once more closely</i>
<i>before we go.</i>

550
01:24:36.988 --> 01:24:39.115
<i>So pretty, our BLINKs.</i>

551
01:24:39.199 --> 01:24:42.827
<i>Please support us</i>
<i>and stay excited till the end.</i>

552
01:24:42.911 --> 01:24:44.329
<i>-We love you.
-We love you.</i>

553
01:24:46.164 --> 01:24:51.002
CROWD: BLACKPINK! BLACKPINK! BLACKPINK!

554
01:24:51.086 --> 01:24:57.675
BLACKPINK! BLACKPINK! BLACKPINK!

555
01:24:58.760 --> 01:25:00.970
(audience cheer)

556
01:25:05.350 --> 01:25:07.143
THANK YOU FOR BEING THE LIGHT OF MY YOUTH

557
01:25:07.393 --> 01:25:09.604
(audience cheer)

558
01:25:10.438 --> 01:25:13.149
(<i>Forever Young</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

559
01:26:12.625 --> 01:26:14.669
(<i>Forever Young</i> continues)

560
01:27:54.811 --> 01:27:57.105
(<i>Forever Young</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

561
01:29:08.468 --> 01:29:10.887
(audience cheer)

562
01:29:14.599 --> 01:29:18.853
(cheering)

563
01:29:29.989 --> 01:29:31.991
(<i>Whistle</i> by BLACKPINK playing)

564
01:30:38.641 --> 01:30:41.060
(<i>Whistle</i> continues)

565
01:32:59.448 --> 01:33:02.076
(audience cheer)

566
01:33:02.410 --> 01:33:09.250
CROWD: BLACKPINK! BLACKPINK! BLACKPINK!

567
01:33:09.333 --> 01:33:15.756
BLACKPINK! BLACKPINK! BLACKPINK!

568
01:33:18.217 --> 01:33:21.846
(in Korean) So may I make it short
and do it with a gesture?

569
01:33:21.929 --> 01:33:23.931
-JENNIE: Sure.
-LISA: Okay, I'll go with my gesture.

570
01:33:24.015 --> 01:33:26.225
-Since everyone expresses differently.
-Right.

571
01:33:26.309 --> 01:33:27.768
